  "text": "Finnabair is an Irish heroine who may also be a goddess. Her mother was Medb, queen of Connacht, and Finnabair shared many of her mother's traits, with a keen sense of personal worth. She loved the hero Fraech, and the pair agreed to meet on an island ringed by a deep pool. Fraech swam naked across the water, and a fierce sea monster attacked him on the way. He could not pay the bride-price Medb and Ailill mac Mata demanded, for they coveted cattle of the Otherworld held in his fortune. Many adventures passed before the two lovers joined. Captors soon hauled Finnabair to a stronghold in the Alps, and Fraech set her free. During the raid on the province of Ulster in the north, Medb offered Finnabair to warriors willing to fight the hero Cuchulainn. Fraech answered as other heroes did and met his death. Finnabair died of grief soon after. She is probably a diminished goddess, like Guinevere, Gwenhwyfar, and Jennifer, who share her name.",
